 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 6,
  "text": "I fixed the BUFGCTRL port connections and the deep Gray-counter paths in RTL. One standards finding remains, and it needs an `architecture.yaml` edit that this role can't make.\n\n- **BUFGCTRL by position:** `u_mux` in `rtl/p6_clkmux_core.sv` now connects every port by name (`.O`, `.I0`, `.I1`, `.S0`, `.S1`, `.CE0`, `.CE1`, `.IGNORE0`, `.IGNORE1`). This should clear the \"connected by position\" finding. I haven't re-run the standards gate on it. The `standards` check in `check` is blocked at the moment (see below).\n- **Timing (RPT-LL-02):** In `rtl/mux_domain.sv` I replaced the 64-bit Gray twin's convert, add and re-encode logic with a toggle-rule Gray counter. The binary check (`prev + 1 == cnt`) and the Gray compare are now pipelined over three register stages. The Gray twin is still coded independently of the binary counter. The error count lags the fault by two extra clocks. I have not run synthesis, so the depth reduction is untested, and I did not check the path from `rst_sr_reg[3]` to `u_rst_m`.\n- **Tests:** Lint passes, and the cocotb simulation passes (Verilator, 1 test).\n- **Not fixed:**\n  - `architecture.yaml` has no `clock_muxes` entry for `u_mux` (inputs `clk_c3` and `clk_b`, selected by SEL, as the spec requires). The architecture is frozen and not mine to edit, so the architecture owner needs to add that entry.\n  - The `standards` check (STD-ARCH-00 / HDL-IF-01) fails with `KeyError: 'id'`. It couldn't read the design, so it never reached the clock-mux rule. I didn't find the cause, and I didn't confirm it is related to the missing `clock_muxes` entry.\n- **Not run:** The final `check` with `names: [\"all\"]` was run at scope `rtl` only, so nothing was checked post-synthesis. It gave 5 pass, 1 partial (`resets`, needs a synthesised design), 1 fail (`standards`, above) and 1 not run (`fastpath`).\n\nDONE"
 },
